    description: "World-renowned museum of Impressionist and Post-Impressionist art",
    category: "Museum",
    detailedDescription: "The Mus\xE9e d'Orsay stands as one of the world's greatest art museums, housed in the spectacular former Gare d'Orsay railway station on the Left Bank of the Seine. This magnificent Beaux-Arts building, with its soaring glass-roofed hall and ornate fa\xE7ade, provides a breathtaking setting for what is widely considered the world's finest collection of Impressionist and Post-Impressionist art. The museum's collection spans the years 1848 to 1914, bridging the gap between the Louvre's classical collections and the Centre Pompidou's modern art, and includes masterworks by Monet, Renoir, Degas, Van Gogh, C\xE9zanne, and countless other luminaries of 19th and early 20th-century art.",
