    historicalInfo: "Park G\xFCell was designed by Antoni Gaud\xED for Eusebi G\xFCell as a garden city project between 1900 and 1914. The project was inspired by the English garden city movement. Only two houses were built, one of which was Gaud\xED's home from 1906 to 1925, now the Gaud\xED House Museum. In 1984, UNESCO designated Park G\xFCell as a World Heritage Site.",
