    narration: "Welcome to Warsaw's Old Town, a UNESCO World Heritage Site that was meticulously reconstructed after World War II. This historic district showcases the resilience and spirit of the Polish people.",
    description: "UNESCO World Heritage Site, meticulously reconstructed after WWII",
    category: "Historic District",
    detailedDescription: "Warsaw's Old Town is the oldest part of the capital city. It was established in the 13th century and was completely destroyed during the Warsaw Uprising in 1944. After World War II, the Old Town was meticulously reconstructed according to pre-war photographs and paintings, particularly those by 18th-century vedutist Bernardo Bellotto. The reconstruction was so thorough and authentic that UNESCO listed Warsaw's Old Town as a World Heritage Site in 1980, citing it as an outstanding example of a near-total reconstruction of a span of history covering the 13th to 20th century. The Old Town is centered on the Old Town Market Place (Rynek Starego Miasta), which teems with restaurants, caf\xE9s, and shops. Surrounding streets feature medieval architecture, the 17th-century Royal Castle, and numerous historical monuments. The area is a popular tourist destination and a symbol of Polish national identity and pride.",
